  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0152\" is a database that stores information about users, posts, images, and user-post comments. It has four tables: User, Post, Image, and User_post_comment.\nThe User table contains information about each user, including their age, gender, interests, name, occupation, password, personal profile, user ID, and username. The User_ID column is the primary key, and the username column is unique.\nThe Post table contains information about each post, including the post ID, title, and description. The Post_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Image table contains information about each image, including the image ID, image URL, and post ID. The Image_ID column is the primary key, and the Post_ID column is a foreign key that references the Post table.\nThe User_post_comment table contains information about each comment made on a post by a user, including the comment content, comment time, post ID, and user ID. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the user ID, post ID, and comment time. The Post_ID and User_ID columns are foreign keys that reference the Post and User tables, respectively.\nThe schema also includes various constraints to ensure data integrity, such as the primary keys and foreign keys. The primary keys ensure that each table has a unique identifier, while the foreign keys ensure that the data in the tables is consistent and accurate. The schema also includes indexes to improve query performance.",
  "gold_question": "This is a Social Media System. For user management, the system maintains users' basic information (user ID, username, password, etc.), records users' personal information (name, gender, age, etc.), and manages users' personalized information (occupation, interests, personal profile). For post management, the system supports users to publish posts, each post contains a title, description and images, and has a unique ID. For comment management, the system supports users to comment on posts, records the comment time and content, and supports viewing all comments on a post.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0152.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0152\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `occupation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `interests` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post` (\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`post_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `image` (\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`image_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `image_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `post` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_post_comment` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `post_id`, `comment_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_post_comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_post_comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `post` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
